{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,ast\nbase=Path('candidate.py').read_text()\nconfig=ast.literal_eval([n.value for n in ast.parse(base).body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets)][-1])\nrefs=['g1-r0020-direct_lifted','g2-r0025-shared_full','g2-r0025-action_context','g2-r0026-compact_slice8','g2-r0027-full_reference_exact','g2-r0027-concentration_direct','g2-r0027-concentration_dense','g2-r0027-overlap_zero']\nheld=['protocol/data hashes','all first-six-day exposures and natural prevalence','3 epochs, batch4096, history128, host seed42','static/history field boundary and complete-pair support','all16 action-age contexts and all16 chronological transition states','embedding width16 and hidden128/64','exact parameter shapes, allocation order and initialization draws','unchanged embedding/pooling, transition and direct lifted gap branches','Adam/lr0.001 and host BCE/scorer','zero overlap input in both new variants']\np={\n 'parent_trial':'g2-r0027-overlap_zero',\n 'study':{\n  'id':'g2-r0028-sparse-collision-sufficiency',\n  'protocol_ref':'9c1635366a72f4c4f67708ee7ae9b72a1b90197ffed3485736388ceff7c91d3e',\n  'evidence_refs':refs,\n  'question':'Can replacing Shannon entropy by collision-derived order-2 entropy preserve the stronger direct_lifted utility at lower cost, after sparse exact counting removes the unused identity-by-context workspace?',\n  'hypothesis':'Observation: g2-r0027-overlap_zero attained AUC0.6303146364, logloss0.1927319603, train619.702s and inference21.883s, versus contemporary full AUC0.6300264948/train630.142s/inference22.291s; concentration was AUC0.630197821 and its dense execution control trained slightly faster, so neither concentration necessity nor reproducible execution savings was established. The full anchor g1-r0020-direct_lifted is AUC0.6304316804. Context coarsening (g2-r0025-action_context) and width8 replacement (g2-r0026-compact_slice8) lost utility. Mechanism hypothesis: within unchanged fine contexts, the already supplied collision C=sum p\"'^2 plus count may carry enough dispersion information that replacing every recurrence Shannon H by H2=-log(C) loses little utility. This removes higher-distribution information and run-level xlogx work, without reducing embedding width or context resolution. A sparse exact Shannon control separates this representation change from compact execution. This is provisional, not a novelty or sufficiency claim.'\"',\n  'nearest_work':[\n   {'source_ref':'trial://g2-r0027-overlap_zero','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Direct parent omits overlap but retains BxLx16 run/context counts and exact Shannon summaries. Both new variants replace that workspace with nested X and (X,Y) runs from one composite sort, using BxL storage; only candidate replaces all recurrence Shannon coordinates with collision-derived H2.'},\n   {'source_ref':'trial://g2-r0027-concentration_direct','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'That replacement changed cross-context overlap G into sqrt(C_i*C_j), keeping Shannon summaries. Its zero control was at least as promising in one run. Here overlap stays zero and the intervention tests Shannon information beyond collision in identity, context and conditional-repeat blocks.'},\n   {'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Primary arXiv1706.06978v4 archived content sha256 5fee25f33f375e51b3ee9417d376ff9dbe2ea3628c932a7679ddfeb0feaaade2, lines219-277 inspected: group pooling and ad-conditioned learned activation are prior components. Local baseline is adapted and normalized, not an exact DIN reproduction. Proposed change concerns empirical recurrence dispersion summaries and sparse execution; it adds no learned event attention. Novelty outside the inspected registry remains unverified.'},\n   {'source_ref':'paper:dmr','verification':'read','difference':'Only author README at commit2c6e76804281954a3c969010a31712cd5054aca9, sha256656c9e5eec79c9843e907a555ede2bf0a66a0db3515916af3d655080057c5a75, lines1-9 inspected. It verifies category/brand/type histories lack item IDs. We use supplied bucket-pair identity, never item identity. Publisher full text is blocked; no detailed architecture or priority claim is supported.'}\n  ],\n  'inherited_components':['Registered full_reference_exact source prefix retained verbatim in each standalone module','All existing trainable modules and initialization; overlap bias-free head retained with zero input','Target-match groups, eligible nonmissing category-brand support, count/collision definitions and log129 scaling','Complete full16 context resolution and original transition/gap computations','No optimizer, auxiliary labels, extra history, custom loss, or cross-batch state'],\n  'proposed_difference':'Composite key64*(category*brand_vocab+brand)+16*match_group+context sorts pair/group before context. Nested run IDs yield joint-pair and pair/context masses in BxL; group and conditional sums use only Bx4 and Bx64. No BxLx16 recurrence array or Gram products occurs in either new forward. exact_sparse keeps empirical Shannon H. collision_sparse replaces all six distinct entropy families (category,brand,pair,context,pair-context,conditional pair) by masked -log(C), while count and C coordinates, feature widths28/28/192 and all parameters remain equal. Higher entropy information is discarded; H2 is redundant with C, so active representational rank is lower despite matched parameter count. Standard entropy/collision mathematics and sparse counting are inherited ideas; no verified new-to-literature claim. A witness n6 counts(3,3) versus(4,1,1) has equal collision1/2 but different Shannon entropy, providing an explicit information-loss counterexample.',\n  'predictions':[\n   'Correctness gate: exact_sparse blocks identity/context/repeat agree with full reference and independent event-equality oracle on <=8 diagnostic rows within2e-6, zero overlap exactly; nested counts conserve complete-pair support exactly. Both variants produce finite logits and correct empty/missing/padded behavior.',\n   'Mechanism gate: collision_sparse changes only entropy coordinate slots; count and collision differences vs exact_sparse are <=2e-6. H2 is nonnegative, zero for empty distributions, and <=Shannon within2e-6. Equal-C/different-Shannon synthetic witness must show discarded information.',\n   'Prospective utility retention: candidate AUC >=0.6299316803980214 (fixed anchor minus0.0005), and candidate minus contemporary exact_sparse AUC >=-0.0005; logloss increase <=0.0002 against both frozen anchor0.19269404064402526 and exact_sparse. These exploratory gates are not statistical equivalence tests.',\n   'Efficiency requires >=5% lower mean measured train time or whole-validation inference time under repeated matched host conditions vs the selected full reference; report p50/p95, parameters, memory, and wall time. Candidate-vs-exact_sparse isolates entropy substitution. A one-run timing decrease or sparse source shape alone is insufficient.',\n   'No parameter reduction is predicted: allocation should remain17253123 for the same meta. Peak GPU memory may remain dominated by embedding optimizer state; no numerical memory or cost improvement is assumed.'\n  ],\n  'falsifiers':[\n   'Any exact-control oracle/conservation/invariance error >2e-6, nonfinite output, support violation or changed nonentropy coordinate invalidates implementation attribution; do not interpret it as scientific evidence against collision sufficiency.',\n   'Candidate fails either predeclared utility margin after permissible paired validation repetitions: this particular entropy replacement does not retain utility. It does not refute all lower-cost mechanisms.',\n   'No reproducible >=5% training or inference reduction falsifies the proposed practical efficiency benefit even if utility is retained. Extra nested-run/scatter overhead can erase saved logs and workspace.',\n   'If exact_sparse also loses utility beyond0.0005 despite passing feature diagnostics, initialization-sensitive arithmetic/training variability remains unresolved and replacement attribution is withheld.'\n  ],\n  'alternative_explanations':['Single-seed noise and floating aggregation/training sensitivity; full source repeats range AUC0.6300265 to0.6307423','Timing/hardware variation: prior concentration_direct and dense trained619.521s and618.338s despite skipped Gram operations','Overlap removal is a common inherited intervention, not an entropy benefit; sparse control and historical full/zero references are needed','Parameter allocations match but H2 is redundant with collision and changes effective capacity/nonlinear features','Sparse nested runs can cost more scalar scatters than dense shared tables; logs may not dominate host end-to-end cost','All conclusions are limited to frozen causal-prefix benchmark and undocumented static-snapshot timing; no production or external-task transfer is established'],\n  'contrasts':[\n   {'parent_ref':'g2-r0027-overlap_zero','intervention':'collision_sparse: all recurrence Shannon entropy slots become H2=-log(C) on sparse exact supports','control':'exact_sparse: same nested-run execution architecture and zero-overlap branch, exact Shannon slots; historical g2-r0027-overlap_zero and full anchor remain secondary comparisons','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['H2 has lower effective information rank despite equal allocated capacity','Branches intentionally omit xlogx work only in candidate; representation and its necessary computation are the defined replacement','GPU floating reduction order and single-seed instability'], 'decision_if_supported':'Retain only as a provisional collision-sufficiency candidate; freeze source/config and closest exact/full comparison before validation repetitions. Attribute utility contrast to entropy substitution within zero-overlap sparse setting; demand repeated measured savings for efficiency.','decision_if_not_supported':'Retain exact sparse control only if correctness, utility and repeated cost support it; otherwise retain stronger full reference. Record candidate loss and identify conditional entropy versus marginal entropy as a next falsifiable question without expanding this suite.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g2-r0027-overlap_zero','intervention':'exact_sparse replaces BxLx16 counts with nested sparse X/XY run masses from one composite sort','control':'Historical g2-r0027-overlap_zero execution and in-checkpoint full/dense feature oracles; no new full training run in this suite','held_fixed':held+['all Shannon/count/collision feature definitions'], 'remaining_confounds':['Historical timing is not concurrent','Arithmetic order may change scratch-training trajectories','No independent backward equivalence check is executable locally without torch'], 'decision_if_supported':'Treat as execution engineering only, never representation mechanism evidence; verify savings in paired host assessment when selected.','decision_if_not_supported':'Do not claim sparse execution improves the frontier; preserve the known full implementation.'}\n  ],\n  'cost_plan':{\n   'estimate_ref':'g2-r0027-full_reference_exact wall734.088s; g2-r0027-overlap_zero wall722.332s; runtime remaining6289.815s, all work charged; protocol estimate704.373s/unit and cap1760.932s remain frozen',\n   'all_variants_counted':True,\n   'attribution_reserve':'Exactly two current host units, ~1500s total at750s/unit: candidate collision_sparse and exact_sparse matched control. Historical full/zero/concentration and failed-direction receipts are reused as preliminary evidence, never as contemporary timing replications. No screening, optimizer search or training in coding jail. Diagnostics are charged with their host calls.',\n   'assessment_reserve':'Target remaining ~4500s for six val