er:dmr','verification':'read','difference':'Only author README at commit2c6e76804281954a3c969010a31712cd5054aca9, sha256656c9e5eec79c9843e907a555ede2bf0a66a0db3515916af3d655080057c5a75, lines1-9 inspected. It verifies category/brand/type histories lack item IDs. We use supplied bucket-pair identity, never item identity. Publisher full text is blocked; no detailed architecture or priority claim is supported.'}\n  ],\n  'inherited_components':['Registered full_reference_exact source prefix retained verbatim in each standalone module','All existing trainable modules and initialization; overlap bias-free head retained with zero input','Target-match groups, eligible nonmissing category-brand support, count/collision definitions and log129 scaling','Complete full16 context resolution and original transition/gap computations','No optimizer, auxiliary labels, extra history, custom loss, or cross-batch state'],\n  'proposed_difference':'Composite key64*(category*brand_vocab+brand)+16*match_group+context sorts pair/group before context. Nested run IDs yield joint-pair and pair/context masses in BxL; group and conditional sums use only Bx4 and Bx64. No BxLx16 recurrence array or Gram products occurs in either new forward. exact_sparse keeps empirical Shannon H. collision_sparse replaces all six distinct entropy families (category,brand,pair,context,pair-context,conditional pair) by masked -log(C), while count and C coordinates, feature widths28/28/192 and all parameters remain equal. Higher entropy information is discarded; H2 is redundant with C, so active representational rank is lower despite matched parameter count. Standard entropy/collision mathematics and sparse counting are inherited ideas; no verified new-to-literature claim. A witness n6 counts(3,3) versus(4,1,1) has equal collision1/2 but different Shannon entropy, providing an explicit information-loss counterexample.',\n  'predictions':[\n   'Correctness gate: exact_sparse blocks identity/context/repeat agree with